  "summary": "After tracing power rails, the CAN/MCP2515 paths (crystals Y2/Y3 read 16 MHz as required, 120R termination present), the ISL54222 USB/serial mux, the LTC4412+P-MOS USB ideal-diode path, the SN74LVC1G07 e-stop sinks feeding the shared ESTOP_OUT/NET0178 net on the CAN connectors, and the WS2812B string, the drawing is internally consistent with the specification. The items I examined that could look wrong (no power-sequencing IC on GLOBAL_EN, the USB ideal-diode arrangement, the unresolved CAN-LED polarity, the absent PCF85063 RTC, the reference-designator reassignments such as U22 being the LIS3MDL magnetometer rather than a buffer) are all either documented open issues/TODOs in the spec or out-of-spec additions the spec explicitly permits, so none constitute a supported deviation. I found no anomaly the drawing clearly supports."
}

